:: Carter Bedroom Relax Cuddle [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> end up lying down on his bed, both feeling a bit tired and needing a minute to rest your body. <span style="color:Pink">You end up shoulder to shoulder, since his bed is only built for one person, though his small size makes it not that uncomfortable. You imagine if sleeping over would result in the two of you sharing a bed, or if he’d be too embarrassed and send one of you to the floor or beanbags. It is a cute though and you roll onto your side and smile at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, who looks awfully sleepy.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Eyes: "Tired",
            },	
        },
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
                Eyes: "Tired",
            },	
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“We- we should get up…”</span> He says through a yawn, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I don’t wanna sleep, come on, let’s…”</span> He yawns again, his eyes feeling heavy. You keep smiling at the boy, his tiredness contagious as you feel your own eyes begin to grow heavier and heavier. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“No…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> mumbles, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Can’t falls asleep, it’s too…”</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    Your eyes open some time later, you’re not sure how long it was, but you fell asleep. <span style="color:Pink">The first thing you see when you wake up is <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s adorably peaceful face. He had rolled onto his side as well, leaving you both face to face, your arms slightly intertwined as you cuddle unconsciously. It’s pretty adorable and your light chuckle seems to stir <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Huh? What-?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> takes a second to process what happened as you teasingly tell him good morning. The confusion on his face lasts a moment before he realizes he had fallen asleep and a look of sheer panic appears on his face. <span style="color:Pink">His cheeks turn red and he practically leaps out of bed.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Ahhh! No!”</span> He seems to frantically do something, before seeming to calm down. He then turns to you with a slightly flustered look, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“S- sorry… I, umm… I didn’t want to fall asleep, since it’s a little embarrassing, but I guess it’s fine. Should- should we play a game or something?”</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 2,
            },	
        },
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },	
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

    The boy seems to have just had his energy spiked and then fallen, making him look like he needs another nap. Though he assures you he’s fine, just wanting to play something and not sleep the playdate away. <span style="color:Yellow">Maybe he had a nightmare or something and is a little embarrassed about it? Weird.</span> <br>

    <span style="color:Green">+Carter Energy</span><br>
    <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy += 10>>
    <<needChange "Energy" 10>>
    <<socialChange "Carter" 1>>
    <br>
